{
  "content": "<p><strong>Description:</strong> Prof. Burge discusses comparative genomics. He begins with a review of global alignment of protein sequences, then talks about Markov models, the Jukes-Cantor model, and Kimura models. He discusses types of selection: natural, negative, and positive.</p>\n<p><strong>Instructor:</strong> Christopher Burge</p>\n",
